// blackvault, coordination-only peer. The Xebia Mac.
//
// Install as ".stignore" in the vault root on a device whose vault content
// arrives over LiveSync instead. Syncthing then carries nothing but the lease
// claims, so the singleton election stays available while the bridge it elects
// is stopped.
//
// Only ever pair this with LiveSync actually enabled on that device. It is an
// allowlist ending in "**", so a host left with this file and no LiveSync has
// no content transport at all, in either direction, and Syncthing still reports
// the folder as in sync.
//
// The leading dot in ".leases" is load-bearing. Syncthing matches "*" against
// dotfiles, so a rule naming the undotted path lets the "Agent State/*" line
// below it swallow the whole lease tree, and the host then reads every role as
// unheld.
//
// Read this bottom-up. First match wins, and un-ignoring a directory only lets
// Syncthing descend into it, so each level has to re-ignore its other children
// before the next "!" line.
!/99 - Meta/Agent State/.leases/**
!/99 - Meta/Agent State/.leases
/99 - Meta/Agent State/*
!/99 - Meta/Agent State
/99 - Meta/*
!/99 - Meta
/*
**
